  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/54536.png\" style=\"width: 380px; height: 219px;\" /><br />Since block doesn't move with respect towedge, so friction force should balance the component of weight along the inclined plane.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math><br /><br />Component of displacement along the inclined plane in time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mi>θ</mi></mfenced></math><br />Work done by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
